@* Lab adaptation (Sprint 33.9, FE33-047): the BeeDay source injects IStringLocalizer<SharedResources>
   for the brand aria-label and CTA label — dropped for plain hardcoded English strings taken
   verbatim from SharedResources.en-US.resx at extraction time ("beeday home", "Continue to
   beeday"), same rule Sprint 33.8 established for every localizer-injecting file it touched.

   The real <AuthorizeView><Authorized>...</Authorized></AuthorizeView> requires a real
   AuthenticationStateProvider, which ADR-008 forbids the Lab from adding (no real authentication
   infrastructure). It is replaced with a plain [Parameter] bool (IsAuthenticatedScenario) toggling
   the same CTA block — Lab-local scenario state instead of real auth, exactly the pattern the
   Sprint 33.9 issue calls for.

   The real AuthenticatedEntryDestinationResolver injection and its NavigationManager-based
   ContinueToBeeDay() (which resolves the signed-in user's real landing route via
   BeeDay.Application) are dropped entirely — the Lab has no such resolver and must not fabricate
   one. ContinueToBeeDay() instead navigates to a fixed local placeholder route ("/"): honestly
   presentation-only, no destination-resolution algorithm invented. *@
<header class="public-header">
    <div class="public-header__content beeday-container">
        <a class="public-header__brand" href="/" aria-label="beeday home">
            <BeeDayBrand Class="public-header__brand-mark" />
        </a>

        <div class="public-header__actions">
            <PublicLanguageSwitcher />
            @if (IsAuthenticatedScenario)
            {
                <BeeDayButton Compact="true" OnClick="ContinueToBeeDay">Continue to beeday</BeeDayButton>
            }
        </div>
    </div>
</header>

@code {
    [Inject] private NavigationManager Navigation { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// Lab-local scenario toggle standing in for the real &lt;AuthorizeView&gt; — set by a Lab
    /// caller/demo to preview the header with or without the "Continue to beeday" CTA, with no real
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider involved.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public bool IsAuthenticatedScenario { get; set; }

    private void ContinueToBeeDay() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/", forceLoad: true, replace: true);
}
